      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is double the maximum, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** This could be 850 mg twice daily with meals, or another split.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nPlease tell me which dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentionally above the maximum. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
